Description: Only what the Darwin library needs is configured and built
 The packages ship only the library, its header, pkg-config file and
 autoconf macro. Without doc/ and tests/ in configure.ac and SUBDIRS,
 automake does not read the manual or the test makefiles. The doc switch
 goes with doc/. Without src/versioninfo.rc and src/libassuan-config,
 configure does not read their templates. m4/Makefile only lists the
 macros for make dist, so it is not configured. In foreign mode automake
 needs no AUTHORS, ChangeLog, INSTALL, NEWS, README or COPYING. AB_INIT
 only logs build details, so autobuild.m4 is not used.
 .
 assuan.h is made from the posix-*.inc.h parts only, as mkheader does for
 Darwin. libSystem has funopen, isascii, stpcpy and setenv, so they are
 checked for but have no replacement sources. memrchr keeps its
 replacement.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
